(NumPy Revision Cheatsheet) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1\) Import + Array Creation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(From list: a = np.array\([1, 2, 3]\)) Tj
T*
(2D array: A = np.array\([[1, 2], [3, 4]]\)) Tj
T*
(Zeros / Ones / Constant:) Tj
T*
(  - np.zeros\(\(m, n\)\)) Tj
T*
(  - np.ones\(\(m, n\)\)) Tj
T*
(  - np.full\(\(m, n\), k\)) Tj
T*
(Range:) Tj
T*
(  - np.arange\(start, stop, step\)) Tj
T*
(  - np.linspace\(start, stop, num\)) Tj
T*
(Identity matrix: np.eye\(n\)) Tj
T*
(Random:) Tj
T*
(  - np.random.rand\(m, n\) \(uniform [0,1\)\)) Tj
T*
(  - np.random.randn\(m, n\) \(normal distribution\)) Tj
T*
(  - np.random.randint\(low, high, size=\(m, n\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Quick reminder: Prefer NumPy arrays over Python lists for numeric operations \(faster +) Tj
T*
(vectorized\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2\) Shape, Dimension, and Data Type) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(a.shape ? tuple of dimensions) Tj
T*
(a.ndim ? number of dimensions) Tj
T*
(a.size ? total number of elements) Tj
T*
(a.dtype ? element type) Tj
T*
(Convert type: a.astype\(np.float64\)) Tj
T*
(Reshape: a.reshape\(r, c\)) Tj
T*
(Flatten: a.ravel\(\) or a.flatten\(\)) Tj
T*
(Transpose: A.T or A.transpose\(\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Formula:) Tj
T*
(total_elements = d1  d2  ...  dk) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Quick reminder: reshape needs same total elements before/after.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
